                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d3b6690-7277-4e92-bc2e-1865a0654505",
                                                "sense_id": "2b375b63-cc26-3d96-94c8-2219d3a2024b",
                                                "text": "Figging is usually considered to indicate a good quality of soft soap, but such is really not the case. A first-class soft soap can be made which will not fig, while, on the other hand, a poor soap can be produced which will fig."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d75ab7a-ffc4-40e7-9360-e164046c18df",
                                                "sense_id": "2b375b63-cc26-3d96-94c8-2219d3a2024b",
                                                "text": "The figging is probably due to the separation of the potash salts of some of the fatty acids having a high solidifying point, i. e., [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "369b39f1-85bd-40bc-baf2-0255deb45ce4",
                                                "sense_id": "2b375b63-cc26-3d96-94c8-2219d3a2024b",
                                                "text": "Artificial figging was at one time produced by dispersing insoluble fillers in the base."
